            <note corresp="#d710a-119-f8" n="8" xml:id="d710a-119-f8-content">
                <p>Cf. the following translation of an undated letter from Gromyko to Dunn (file No.
                    740.00119 Potsdam/7–2845): <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I am sending you herewith the text of the protocol entries on questions
                            raised at the Conference by the Soviet Delegation.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>The attachment to this letter, however, consists, not of “entries” on questions
                    raised by the Soviet Delegation, but of a Russian text of sections <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">i</hi> and <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi> A of
                        <ref target="#d1383">document No. 1383</ref>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >post</hi>. Cf. <ref target="#d1343">documents Nos. 1343</ref>, <ref
                        target="#d1426">1426</ref>, <ref target="#d1428">1428</ref>, and <ref
                        target="#d1430">1430</ref>–<ref target="#d1433">1433</ref>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">post</hi>.</p>
            </note>
